--Project title--
Netflix Movies & TV Shows Data Analysis

--Project Description--
This project analyzes the Netfliz dataset to explore trends in content type,
release patterns.movie durations, TV show seasons, and overall platform growth.
It includes data cleaning, preprocessing, visualization, and insights.

--Dataset Information--
Dataset: netflix_titles.csv
Rows: ~6,000+
Columns: title, director, cast, country, rating, date_added, duraion, etc.
Source: Kaggle (Netflix Title Dataset)

--Project workflow--
1.Importing libraris
2.Loading dataset
3.Data cleaning and preprocessing
    -Handling missing values
    -Removing duplicates
    -converting date format
    -Extracting year & month
4.Exploratory Data Analysis (6 graphs)
5.key insights and summary  

--Visualization--
1. Bar chart - Movies vs TV Shows country
2. Pie chart - Content type distribution
3. Line chart - Yearly content growth
4. Bar chart - Monthly content addition
5. Histogram - Movie duration distribution
6. Bar chart - TV show seasons country

--key insights--
- Netflix has more Movies than TV Shows.
- Upload trend increased significantly after 2015.
- Most movies are between 80–120 minutes.
- TV Shows typically have 1–3 seasons.
- Content is uploaded consistently every month.

--Technologies Used--
Python
Pandas
Matplotlib
NumPy

--How to Run the Project--
1. Install required libraries:
   pip install pandas matplotlib numpy

2. Place netflix_titles.csv in the project folder

3. Run:
   python netflix_analysis.py

--Conclusion--
This analysis gives a clear overview of Netflix’s content strategy 
and user consumption patterns.

